  "summary": "Five preprints show bias-aware and uncertainty-aware learning from sequence, structure and graphs across enzymes, glycans, docking and adverse-event prediction.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is predictive modelling of biomolecular function from sequence, structure or graph representations, with explicit handling of representation limits. CarmnaDD predicts nitrogenase activity from sequence alone with dual descriptors (R2 0.60, AUC 0.94) and maps informative windows onto NifH. SCOPE combines structure and evolutionary information in a residue-level graph model for catalytic residues, with mutagenesis validation. GlycanPUG applies heterogeneous graph pretraining on WURCS 2.0 to structurally ambiguous glycans. Two preprints address reliability: Inverse Node Frequency normalises metapath features to reduce hub bias in target-adverse event prediction, and a dependence-aware conformal framework with copula calibration provides 3D uncertainty intervals for docking. The new element is interpretability, debiasing and calibrated uncertainty added to predictors.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-26"
}
